  "uprn": "10091693887",
  "decision_date": "06/12/2022",
  "description": "Retrospective Variation of condition 2 (approved plans) to allow changes of the dry brick walls across the site to reclaimed bricks and natural materials encased in gabion baskets with alterations to the widths and heights of walls, ground levels in The Observatory and Educational Enclosure areas, and minor changes to the positioning and sizing of The Observatory area, surfaced paths widened to a minimum of 1.5m and mown grass paths will be 1.2m, inclusion of tactile paving and hand rails in The Observatory area and balustrades to the decking by the tidal inlet, for proposed landscape, habitat enhancement and community amenity improvements on the site and along the left bank of the adjoining River Crane following planning permission 00809/E/P1 approved 24/12/2020 for the proposed landscape, habitat enhancement and community amenity improvements on the site and along the left bank of the adjoining River Crane.",
  "site_name": "Land At",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "06/12/2022",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "Northcote Avenue",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "lapsed_date": "05/12/2025",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of the original planning permission i.e. 24/12/2020.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted ([Cover Letter], [MH-8472/003], Received: 11/10/2022, [MH-8472/001/A], [MH-8472/002/A], [101], Received: 15/11/2022) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Excavation and Contamination\r\nThe work shall be carried out in accordance with the Excavation and Soil Strategy Statement (Doc ref. 0091/081) submitted under application 00809/E/P1 and the findings of the Phase 2 Intrusive Site Investigation submitted with the application hereby approved \r\nLevels of contamination shall be sampled and monitored throughout the soil movement phases of the project and if this reveals levels of contamination higher than previously predicted or identified, revised remediation measures shall be devised and submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority before the affected part of the approved project is allowed to continue.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Wheelchair accessibility \r\nNotwithstanding the approved plans, before the development hereby approved is first brought into use, a flat landing with a minimum depth of 1.5 metres shall be installed to the pedestrian foot ramp to 'The Observatory' area. Any stair riser shall be no more than 170 millimetres in height."
  ],
